<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Eluma buys Marvin for $15 mln - paper.</title>
<headline>Brazil Eluma buys Marvin for $15 mln - paper.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian metal company Eluma concluded Thursday the purchase of Grupo Arbi's Marvin, newspapers reported Friday.</p>
<p>The deal, estimated at $15 million, is part of Eluma's growth strategy, they said.</p>
<p>Jornal do Brasil said Eluma now negotiates the sale of up to 40 percent of its capital to Europa Metalli group.</p>
<p>Eluma is Brazil's largest semi-elaborated copper products maker. Marvin is the fourth company sold by Grupo Arbi, controlled by businesman Daniel Birmann, Gazeta Mercantil said.</p>
<p>-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom 55-11-2324411</p>
